    <string name="import_hint_accounts">CSV for accounts:\nAccountName,AccountComment,AccountIconName,CurrencyName,CurrencyIso,CurrencyIconName\nElectronics,Electronics,unknown,,,\nEuro cash,Cash in euros,unknown,EUR,EUR,unknown</string>
    <string name="import_hint_operations">CSV for operations:\nDate,AccountFr,AccountTo,Amount,Comment\n2020-09-26,Cash,Café,7,Tea at \"Tarantino\" café\n2020-09-01,Salary,Cash,1000000,Salary</string>
    <string name="import_hint_rates">CSV for rates:\nSymbol,Date,Rate\nEURRUB,2020-09-12,88.5101\nEURUSD,2020-08-20,1.18023\nEURUSD,2020-08-22,1.17544</string>
    <string name="import_hint_json">Handles transfers and fees — CSV can\'t do that — as well as accounts\nwith a currency, currency pairs and rates in one file; all sections are optional:\n{\n  \"accounts\": [\n    {\"name\": \"USD card\", \"comment\": \"...\", \"icon\": \"Visa card\",\n     \"currency\": {\"name\": \"USD\", \"iso\": \"USD\", \"icon\": \"\"}}\n  ],\n  \"currency_pairs\": [{\"symbol\": \"EURUSD\", \"base\": \"EUR\", \"quote\": \"USD\"}],\n  \"rates\": [{\"symbol\": \"EURUSD\", \"date\": \"2020-08-20\", \"rate\": 1.18023}],\n  \"operations\": [\n    {\"date\": \"2020-08-26\", \"from\": \"Card\", \"to\": \"USD card\",\n     \"amount\": 5000, \"comment\": \"\",\n     \"leg\": {\"amount\": 65.4},\n     \"commission\": {\"amount\": 50, \"from\": \"source\", \"category\": \"Transfer commission\"}},\n    {\"date\": \"2020-08-26\", \"from\": \"Groceries\", \"to\": \"Card\",\n     \"amount\": 1200, \"comment\": \"\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nThe old format (a bare array — operations only) is read as well.\n\"leg\"/\"commission\" are optional; without them it\'s a plain entry, like in CSV.\n\"commission.from\" is \"source\" or \"dest\", \"source\" by default.</string>

